WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.450
OT architecture should make communication deliberate.

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:08.325
The Purdue model is a useful mental model for discussing layers of an industrial environment.

00:00:08.325 --> 00:00:13.026
At lower levels are the physical process, sensors, actuators, and basic control.

00:00:13.026 --> 00:00:16.159
Above them are supervisory systems and operations management.

00:00:16.159 --> 00:00:20.859
Enterprise services sit higher, with an industrial demilitarized zone, or industrial DMZ,

00:00:20.859 --> 00:00:23.210
often separating business and operational networks.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:27.518
The model is not a perfect map of every modern facility.

00:00:27.518 --> 00:00:29.868
Cloud services, wireless devices, vendor connections,

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:32.610
and distributed sites can cross traditional boundaries.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:37.702
Its value is that it forces teams to ask which functions belong together,

00:00:37.702 --> 00:00:41.227
where trust changes, and which communications are actually required.

00:00:41.227 --> 00:00:44.752
Segmentation limits unnecessary connectivity between enterprise IT, operations systems,

00:00:44.752 --> 00:00:46.711
control networks, and field devices.

00:00:46.711 --> 00:00:51.411
A well-designed boundary permits documented business flows while reducing the ability of

00:00:51.411 --> 00:00:54.936
an incident to move directly toward critical control assets.

00:00:54.936 --> 00:00:58.462
Rules should be based on known sources, destinations, protocols,

00:00:58.462 --> 00:01:01.595
and operational purpose rather than broad network access.

00:01:01.595 --> 00:01:07.470
An industrial DMZ can host services that exchange information across the IT and OT boundary,

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.604
such as patch staging, remote-access gateways, replication services,

00:01:10.604 --> 00:01:12.171
or intermediary data transfer.

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:16.479
This avoids direct connections from ordinary enterprise endpoints to control systems.

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:19.613
The DMZ is not protective by name alone.

00:01:19.613 --> 00:01:21.963
Services must be hardened, monitored, maintained,

00:01:21.963 --> 00:01:25.880
and configured so they do not become an uncontrolled bridge.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.838
Segmentation also applies within OT.

00:01:27.838 --> 00:01:30.188
Separate sites, production cells, safety-related functions,

00:01:30.188 --> 00:01:33.714
and management interfaces when risk and operations justify it.

00:01:33.714 --> 00:01:39.981
Avoid assuming that every device on an internal control network should communicate with every other device.

00:01:39.981 --> 00:01:44.289
At the same time, changes must preserve required timing, redundancy, troubleshooting,

00:01:44.289 --> 00:01:45.464
and failover behavior.

00:01:45.464 --> 00:01:47.814
The practical objective is controlled connectivity.

00:01:47.814 --> 00:01:51.339
Maintain current diagrams, document approved flows, monitor boundary traffic,

00:01:51.339 --> 00:01:54.865
review temporary access, and test rule changes with engineers.

00:01:54.865 --> 00:02:00.740
Good architecture reduces exposure and creates useful detection points without making the physical operation brittle.
